{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/708613-some-questions-about-fighting-and-stuff-werewolf-the-forsaken","id":708613,"title":"Some questions about fighting and stuff (Werewolf : The Forsaken)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-19T06:01:54-07:00","id":708613,"title":"Some questions about fighting and stuff (Werewolf : The Forsaken)","content":"Hello everyone ! <br /> This is about Werewolf : The Forsaken. <br /> <br /> I have trouble with how to deal with some stuff during a fight. My game master and one of the players had an argument during our last game, mainly because in France we don't have every book to help us with the rules (either they're not published anymore or we cannot find anything online...)<br /> So here are my questions : how do you dodge ? What characteristics (attributes ?) do you add ? Is it a good idea to re-use the rules from Vampire : The Masquerade if there's nothing about that anywhere ? <br /> <br /> I know my question might seem a bit stupid, but it seems we are stuck. If you need any further info about the fight we were in, I'll explain : )<br /> Thanks !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8681-bluehilde","name":"Bluehilde","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T06:12:19-07:00","id":708650,"title":"","content":"First edition or second? They changed how it works slightly when they updated the rules. <br /> <br /> In both editions the standard dodge manoeuvre simply doubles your defense value. In first edition this doubled value is just taken from the opponent's attack pool, while in second edition it is rolled against the attacker's and each success cancels out one of theirs. Get it to zero, they miss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T06:27:26-07:00","id":708670,"title":"","content":"Oh my gods, thanks so much ! <br /> I've got another question, does dodging count as a move (like an standard attack, as a punch in the face or something ?) and can we choose not to dodge ? (sorry for all the &quot;beginners&quot; questions o_o&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8681-bluehilde","name":"Bluehilde","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T06:46:18-07:00","id":708691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluehilde</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/708613-some-questions-about-fighting-and-stuff-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=708670#post708670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh my gods, thanks so much !<br /> I've got another question, does dodging count as a move (like an standard attack, as a punch in the face or something ?) and can we choose not to dodge ? (sorry for all the &quot;beginners&quot; questions o_o&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two ways to avoid being hit:<br /> <br /> Defense is a passive value that always applies to any non-Firearm attack (so Brawl, Weaponry, car crashes, etc...). It simply subtracts from the attacker's attack pool. You can choose not to apply your Defense against an attack.<br /> <br /> Dodging is an action that you have to declare that you're doing, and it takes up your turn (so you can't also run, attack, or anything else).<br /> <br /> In 1st Edition NWoD, Dodging doubles your Defense and is applied <i><b>before</b></i> the attacker rolls.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Example:</i></b><i>The psycho with a chainsaw attacks with 13 (Strength + Weaponry + Chainsaw damage + Willpower + All-out Attack) dice. You decide to Dodge. Your Defense is normally 2 (lower of Wits or Dexterity), so you double it and subtract 4 from the attacker's roll, which reduces it to 7. They roll and the number of successes they achieve is how much damage is dealt.</i><br /> <br /> In 2nd Edition NWoD, Dodging works differently. You don't subtract your Defense from the attacker's roll, but you roll double your Defense and for each success you get, you remove a success from the attacker <b><i>after</i></b> they roll.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Example: </i></b><i>The psycho with a chainsaw attacks with 9 dice (Strength + Weaponry + Willpower + All-out Attack). You decide to Dodge. Your Defense is normally 4 (lower of Wits or Dexterity + Athletics), so your Dodge roll will be 8. You roll 3 successes each, so they miss.</i><br /> <br /> I hope that clears things up.<br /> <br /> If you choose to Dodge <i>before</i> you perform an action, you can't do anything when your turn comes around (since you're Dodging). If you went before the attacker and did something, you can't Dodge (since you already acted this turn). If you want to Dodge but you're going before the attacker, you have to declare that you'll be spending your turn Dodging.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And don't worry about asking questions. If the books weren't translated into my first language, I'd probably be asking a lot of questions like this too. @_@","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T13:11:36-07:00","id":711154,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the information ! I'm glad we're going to be able to finish that damn fight (and probably die or something... xD)<br /> <br /> Also, just out of curiosity : is there a book, with more complete rules that I can find somewhere (even in english, I don't mind and the game master either) ? : )<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8681-bluehilde","name":"Bluehilde","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T13:33:11-07:00","id":711190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/145541/Werewolf-the-Forsaken-2nd-Edition\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4261/145541.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/145541/Werewolf-the-Forsaken-2nd-Edition\" target=\"_blank\"> Werewolf: the Forsaken 2nd Edition - Onyx Path Publishing | Werewolf: The Forsaken 2nd Edition | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/145541/Werewolf-the-Forsaken-2nd-Edition\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/145541/Werewolf-the-Forsaken-2nd-Edition </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Werewolf: the Forsaken 2nd Edition - The need to hunt burns in your heart and in your soul. To chase down prey with your blood pumping fire through your body </div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> That's the link to Forsaken's second edition. It is a complete rule book (so you can play with just it, no other books needed). Obviously you can get the PDF instantly, but you can also order a print copy if that's more to your liking.<br /> <br /> The same website has lots of other books (though most of the other Forsaken material is going to be 1e focused). The Godmachine Chronciles Rules Update PDF, which is a free download of the 2e rules updates from 1e, can be useful as it has more of some things. Likewise other 2e books (Demon the Descent, Requiem 2e, the upcoming nWOD 2e core book, Mortal Remains) will have material in it that can be useful even if you're not running those games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}